  m_Name: Danaus
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: Assembly-CSharp::ButterflyData
  speciesName: Danaus plexippus
  description: "La Danaus plexippus es una mariposa perteneciente al g\xE9nero Danaus
    y a la familia Nymphalidae. Es conocida por su color vibrante y su gran tama\xF1o.\r\n\r\nCaracter\xEDsticas
    principales:\r\n\r\nEnvergadura: Alcanza una envergadura de 9 a 10 cm, lo que
    la convierte en una mariposa de tama\xF1o considerable.\r\nEl dorso de sus alas
    es de un color naranja brillante con manchas negras, mientras que el reverso
    de las alas tiene una combinaci\xF3n de tonos m\xE1s apagados con detalles en
    blanco y marr\xF3n.\r\nEs muy similar en apariencia a la famosa Danaus plexippus
    (mariposa monarca), pero con patrones de color ligeramente diferentes."
  speciesNameEn: Butterfly Danaus plexippus (Monarch)
  descriptionEn: 'The Danaus plexippus  is a butterfly belonging to the genus Danaus
    and the family Nymphalidae . It is known for its vibrant color and large size.

    

    Main
    features:

    

    Wingspan: It reaches a wingspan of 9 to 10 cm , which
    makes it a butterfly of considerable size.

    The back of its wings is a bright
    orange color with black spots , while the underside of the wings has a combination
    of more muted tones with white and brown details.

    It is very similar in
    appearance to the famous Danaus plexippus (monarch butterfly), but with slightly
    different color patterns.'
